         measured: linear power deviates by 0.0299, flux power by 0.0457, response 1.53; filtered-field variance sigma^2 = 1.673
         reading : the response is not a suppression. Projecting three dimensions onto one puts power from every transverse mode with q >= k into the line-of-sight bin at k, so a three-dimensional suppression that begins beyond the forest's reach still shows up inside it, and the nonlinear mapping does not undo that. The flux is MORE sensitive than the linear power at these wavenumbers, not less
  [PASS] V6 [and at the old reach the forest gate is passed after all] the flux-power deviation is compared with the precision of the two kinds of forest measurement, at the reach L194 originally set and L224 reported as failing on linear power
